course: dictionary
lesson: 9770
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. The word surf can mean the white waves on the shore, or the sport of riding those waves on a board. Read the clues around it to choose.
explain: «The surf was high, so the lifeguards put up the red flag.» Here surf means the waves, because you cannot ride a board in the surf when it is high and dangerous, and the flag is about the sea. Ask: is the sentence about water, a board, a website or the TV? That tells you the meaning.
explain: On a screen, surf means something new. «I like to surf the web after school» means you look quickly from one website to another, which is another word for browse. The same word belongs to a different world, and the context shows which world you are in.
fact: Surf is a noun and a verb. As a noun it means the white, foamy waves that break on the shore.
fact: As a verb, surf means to ride on waves standing or lying on a board, and it changes: surf, surfs, surfed, surfing, as in «I was surfing all morning».
fact: «Surf the web» or «surf the internet» means to look quickly from one website to another.
fact: «Channel-surf» is informal and means to change TV channels quickly.
fact: In French, «je fais du surf» means I go surfing. If you don't know the verb for a sport, say faire de plus the sport.
exercise: «The surf was heavy, so we swam between the flags.» What is the surf here? | A website | A TV channel | *The white, foamy waves that break on the shore | A board for riding the waves
exercise: «I like to surf the web after school.» What does surf mean here? | To ride on a board in the sea | *To look quickly from one website to another | To swim very far out | To change the TV channel
exercise: Ana says, «Je fais du surf.» What does it mean? | I eat fish by the sea | *I go surfing | I make a surf of the sea | I watch the waves from the beach
test: «Dad says the surf's up, so grab your board!» What is the surf? | *The waves, ready for riding | A website full of pages | A TV channel | A kind of sandwich
test: Mia says, «I channel-surf until bedtime.» What does it mean? | Cooks dinner for the family | Reads a long book in bed | Swims in the sea until dark | *Changes TV channels quickly
exam: Which sentence uses surf as a verb? | *I want to surf tomorrow | Heavy surf hit the rocks | Lifesavers watch the surf from the tower | The surf was loud and wild
